{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/dijkstrasearchevent"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DijkstraSearchEvent"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"DijkstraSearch.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ShortestPaths\/DijkstraSearch.swift#L17"},"roleHeading":"Enumeration","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"enum","modules":[{"name":"ShortestPaths"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DijkstraSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:13ShortestPaths19DijkstraSearchEventO","title":"DijkstraSearchEvent"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DijkstraSearchEvent"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Weight"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each source is discovered first, at distance zero. Then, while a discovered vertex is not yet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"settled, the one with the smallest distance is examined (settled at that distance), and each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of its out-edges is examined in turn with the distance it offers its target: the examined","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex’s distance plus the edge’s weight. An edge into an unsettled target is then relaxed,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when the offer is smaller than the target’s distance or the target was not yet discovered, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not relaxed. A relaxed edge to an undiscovered target is followed by that target’s discovery.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"An edge into a settled vertex, a self-loop included, is examined and nothing more. After its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"last out-edge the examined vertex is finished. Vertices the sources do not reach are never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/DijkstraSearchEvent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/SQ","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/SH","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"What a Dijkstra search reports, in order, with the events of the Boost Graph Library’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Dijkstra visitor.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"title":"Enumeration Cases","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/DijkstraSearchEvent\/discover(_:distance:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/DijkstraSearchEvent\/edgeNotRelaxed(_:distance:)","doc:\/\/Shorte